# Test: a read-only web user is denied GET /config/download (403).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-bcrypt-hash-credential AC-4 -- GET /config/download is
#            gated by RequireEditAuthz (editWrap), so a read-only session cannot
#            fetch the raw committed config (which carries the real bcrypt hash).
#            An edit-authorized user still gets the byte-exact raw file (AC-6).
# PREVENTS: a read-only web user exfiltrating the raw config and its password
#           hash through the download endpoint.
#
# SKIP RATIONALE: same limitation as web-rbac-readonly.wb -- the runner seeds a
# single zefs local admin, so a *distinct* read-only web login needs config-file
# authz users + profile assignments the --web-only appliance does not provision.
# The gate itself is proven at the Go tier:
#   internal/component/web/handler_config_transfer_test.go
#     TestConfigDownloadRouteGatedByEditAuthz (read-only 403, edit 200 raw)
#   internal/component/web/rbac_test.go
#     TestRouteGateDeniesReadOnly / TestRouteGateAllowsAdmin

option=skip:reason=needs a config-file read-only web user; zefs seeds only the single local admin (see web-rbac-readonly.wb). Gate proven at Go tier: TestConfigDownloadRouteGatedByEditAuthz
option=timeout:value=30s
option=auth:user=noc:password=ze-web-noc:role=read-only

action=login:user=noc:password=ze-web-noc
action=open:path=/config/download
expect=element:text=forbidden
